  "raw": "The Snake game is complete. Here's a summary:\n\n---\n\n## Snake Game — `deliverables/snake_game/`\n\n**Files:**\n- `main.cpp` — Full game source (~300 lines)\n- `CMakeLists.txt` — CMake build config\n- `build/Release/snake_game.exe` — Compiled executable\n\n**Features:**\n- **Board:** 40×20 play area with double-line box-drawing borders\n- **Controls:** Arrow keys or WASD to steer, P to pause, R to restart, Q to quit\n- **Snake:** Starts with 3 segments, grows when eating food (`*`)\n- **Scoring:** +10 per food eaten, speed increases gradually\n- **High score:** Persisted to `snake_highscore.dat`\n- **Collision:** Walls and self-collision end the game\n- **Game over screen:** Shows final score, high score, restart/quit options\n- **Flicker-free rendering:** Frame built as a single string before output\n\n**How to build (from `deliverables/snake_game/`):**\n```\ncmake -B build -G \"Visual Studio 17 2022\" -A x64\ncmake --build build --config Release\n```\n\n**How to run:**\n```\nbuild\\Release\\snake_game.exe\n```"
}